    "city": "majuro",
    "climate": "tropical-maritime",
    "vernacular": "Narrow coral-atoll strip (highest point under 3 m) with a single road along the island. Ordinary buildings are one- or two-storey concrete-block boxes, plastered and painted in whites, pale blues and yellows or left bare grey, under low-pitched corrugated metal roofs in red, green, blue or galvanised silver; stores and offices are flat-roofed concrete boxes with shop awnings; a few timber-and-thatch jaki-ed style open shelters survive. Crushed-coral and sand ground, dense coconut palms and breadfruit.",
